bi.org.in/Scripts/BS_PressReleaseDisplay.aspx?prid=33496" class="link1" target="_blank">Press Release No. 2014-2015/1971 dated March 19, 2015</a>. </p></div><div class="mmo_div">    <p align="justify">        <sup>#</sup> As per the <a href="https://www.rbi.org.in/Scripts/BS_PressReleaseDisplay.aspx?prid=56998" class="link1" target="_blank">Press Release No. 2023-2024/1548 dated December 27, 2023</a>. </p></div><div class="mmo_div">    <p align="justify">^ As per the <a href="https://www.rbi.org.in/Scripts/NotificationUser.aspx?Id=13224&Mode=0" class="link1" target="_blank">notification No. RBI/2025-26/148 DOR.RET.REC.354/12.01.001/2025-26 dated December 11, 2025</a>.</p></div><div class="mmo_div">    <p align="right">        <b>Ajit Prasad</b>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<br>Deputy General Manager <br>(Communications)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p></div><div class="mmo_div">    <p align="justify"><b>Press Release: 2026-2027/1276</b></p></div>]]></description><link>https://www.rbi.org.in/scripts/BS_PressReleaseDisplay.aspx?prid=63754</link><pubDate>Thu, 08 Oct 2026 09:00:00</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[RBI to conduct 29-day Variable Rate Reverse Repo (VRRR) auction under LAF]]></title><description><![CDATA[<table width="100%" border="0" align="center" class="td"><tr><td><p>On a review of the current and evolving liquidity conditions, it has been decided to conduct a Variable Rate Reverse Repo (VRRR) auction on Thursday, October 08, 2026, as under:</p>  <table width="90%" border="0" align="center" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="1" class="tablebg">    <tr class="head">      <td width="5%" align="center">Sl. No.</td>      <td width="30%" align="center">Notified Amount<br>          (&#8377; crore)</td>      <td width="15%" align="center">Tenor<br>          (day)</td>      <td width="25%" align="center">Window Timing </td>      <td width="25%" align="center">Date of Reversal</td>        </tr>    <tr>      <td align="center" valign="top">1</td>      <td align="center" valign="top">2,00,000</td>      <td align="center" valign="top">29</td>      <td align="center" valign="top">9:30 AM to 10:00 AM</td>      <td align="center" valign="top">November 06, 2026<br>        (Friday)</td>        </tr>      </table><p>2. The operational guidelines for the auction will be same as given in Reserve Bank&rsquo;s <a href="https://www.rbi.org.in/Scripts/BS_PressReleaseDisplay.aspx?prid=49399" target="_blank" class="links">Press Release 2019-2020/1947 dated February 13, 2020</a>.</p><p>3. Participants will have an option for premature reversal of the amount lent in the above auction, and the operational guidelines for the same are as given below:</p><ol type="i">  <li>    <p>Requests for premature reversal can be placed only through the E-Kuber portal during 09:00&ndash;17:00 hours on working days in Mumbai.</p>  </li>  <li>    <p>Partial reversal of a bid will be allowed.</p>  </li>  <li>    <p>Once a request for premature reversal is placed in E-Kuber portal, the same has also to be intimated via <a href="mailto:laffmd@rbi.org.in" class="links">email</a> to the Financial Markets Operations Department (Ph: 022-2263 0982 / 2263 0008). </p>  </li>  <li>    <p>The settlement of premature reversal will take place at the &lsquo;start of day&rsquo; on the next working day following the date of placement of request.</p>  </li>  <li>    <p>On the date of reversal, current account of the participant with the Reserve Bank will be credited with the amount of principal and accrued interest for the lent period. The securities offered as collateral by the RBI will be debited from the participant&rsquo;s reverse repo constituent SGL account.</p>  </li>  <li>    <p>  Request for premature reversal can be placed at least two working days prior to the original date of reversal.</p>  </li>  </ol><p align="right"><span class="head">Ajit Prasad</span>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<br>  Deputy General Manager<br>  (Communications)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p class="head">Press Release: 2026-2027/1275</p></td></tr></table>]]></description><link>https://www.rbi.org.in/scripts/BS_PressReleaseDisplay.aspx?prid=63753</link><pubDate>Wed, 07 Oct 2026 19:10:00</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[Reserve Money for the fortnight ended on September 30, 2026]]></title><description><![CDATA[<table width="100%" border="0" align="center" class="td">  <tr>    <td><p>The Reserve Bank has today released data on <a href="https://rbidocs.rbi.org.in/rdocs/content/docs/PRRM07102026.xlsx" target="_blank" class="links">Reserve Money</a> for the fortnight ended on September 30, 2026.</p>      <p align="right"><span class="head">Ajit Prasad</span>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<br>        Deputy General Manager<br>        (Communications)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>    <p class="head">Press Release: 2026-2027/1274</p></td>  </tr></table>]]></description><link>https://www.rbi.org.in/scripts/BS_PressReleaseDisplay.aspx?prid=63752</link><pubDate>Wed, 07 Oct 2026 17:35:00</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[Exclusion of “Paytm Payments Bank Limited” from the Second Schedule to the Reserve Bank of India Act, 1934]]></title><description><![CDATA[<table width="100%" border="0" align="center" class="td">  <tr>    <td><p>Paytm Payments Bank Limited has been excluded from the Second Schedule to the Reserve Bank of India Act, 1934 vide Notification DoR.LIC.No.S3674/16.13.215/2026-27 dated July 31, 2026 and published in the Gazette of India (Part III - Section 4) dated September 07, 2026.</p>      <p align="right"><span class="head">(Brij Raj)</span>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<br>        Chief General Manager</p>      <p class="head">Press Release: 2026-2027/1273</p></td>  </tr></table>]]></description><link>https://www.rbi.org.in/scripts/BS_PressReleaseDisplay.aspx?prid=63751</link><pubDate>Wed, 07 Oct 2026 17:30:00</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[RBI issues Amendment Directions on 'Standardised Approach for Counterparty Credit Risk (SA-CCR)’]]></title><description><![CDATA[<table width="100%" border="0" align="center" class="td"><tr><td><p>The Reserve Bank of India had issued draft Amendment Directions on the &lsquo;<a href="https://www.rbi.org.in/scripts/BS_PressReleaseDisplay.aspx?prid=62908" target="_blank" class="links">Standardised Approach for Counterparty Credit Risk (SA-CCR)&rsquo; on June 10, 2026</a>, inviting feedback from stakeholders until July 1, 2026. The draft Amendment Directions proposed modifications to the instructions on capital charge for counterparty credit risk as provided in Master Direction on Forthcoming Instructions for commercial banks. Key revisions included: (i) clarifying the scope of CCR for both banking and trading book exposures, (ii) addressing treatment of multiple margin agreements and multiple netting sets in light of recent legal / regulatory developments, (iii) providing guidance for transactions where a bank acts as a clearing member of SEBI-recognised stock exchanges in the equity derivatives and commodity derivatives segments, (iv) specifying the treatment for deferment of option premium, (v) offering guidance on computing effective notional for options, and (vi) including disclosure templates for SA-CCR.</p>  <p>2. Feedback received on the draft instructions has been examined and consequent modifications have been suitably incorporated in the final Amendment Directions. Statement on the feedback received on the draft instructions is provided in the <a href="https://rbidocs.rbi.org.in/rdocs/content/pdfs/PR127207102026_A.pdf" target="_blank" class="links">Annex</a>.</p>  <p>3. Accordingly, the Reserve Bank has today released the <a href="https://rbi.org.in/scripts/NotificationUser.aspx?Id=13730&Mode=0" target="_blank" class="links">Reserve Bank of India (Commercial Banks &ndash; Forthcoming Instructions) Amendment Directions, 2026</a>.</p>  <p>4. These instructions will come into effect from April 1, 2027.</p>  <p align="right"><span class="head">(Brij Raj)</span>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<br>    Chief General Manager</p>  <p class="head">Press Release: 2026-2027/1272</p></td></tr></table>]]></description><link>https://www.rbi.org.in/scripts/BS_PressReleaseDisplay.aspx?prid=63750</link><pubDate>Wed, 07 Oct 2026 17:25:00</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[RBI issues Directions on 'Credit Valuation Adjustment (CVA) Framework’]]></title><description><![CDATA[<table width="100%" border="0" align="center" class="td"><tr>    <td><p>The Reserve Bank of India had issued draft Directions on the &lsquo;<a href="https://www.rbi.org.in/scripts/BS_PressReleaseDisplay.aspx?prid=63314" target="_blank" class="links">Credit Valuation Adjustment (CVA) Framework&rsquo; on August 7, 2026</a>, inviting feedback from stakeholders until August 28, 2026.</p>      <p>2. The draft Directions proposed modifications to the instructions on capital charge for CVA risk for commercial banks. Key revisions included: (i) allowing eligible banks to choose a simpler approach; (ii) increasing the sensitivity of supervisory risk weights for counterparties by sector and credit quality; (iii) clarifying the eligibility and recognition of CVA hedges; and (iv) separate systematic and idiosyncratic CVA risk components in the full Basic Approach (BA-CVA) calculation, addressing imperfect alignment of indirect CVA hedges.</p>      <p>3. Feedback received on the draft instructions has been examined and consequent modifications have been suitably incorporated in the final Directions. Statement on the feedback received on the draft instructions is provided in the <a href="https://rbidocs.rbi.org.in/rdocs/content/pdfs/PR127107102026_AN.pdf" target="_blank" class="links">Annex</a>.</p>      <p>4. Accordingly, the Reserve Bank has today released the <a href="https://www.rbi.org.in/scripts/BS_ViewMasDirections.aspx?id=13729" target="_blank" class="links">Reserve Bank of India (Commercial Banks &ndash; Credit Valuation Adjustment Framework) Directions, 2026</a>.</p>      <p>5. These instructions will come into effect from April 1, 2027.</p>      <p align="right"><span class="head">(Brij Raj)</span>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<br>      Chief General Manager</p>      <p class="head">Press Release: 2026-2027/1271</p></td></tr></table>]]></description><link>https://www.rbi.org.in/scripts/BS_PressReleaseDisplay.aspx?prid=63749</link><pubDate>Wed, 07 Oct 2026 17:05:00</pubDate></item></channel></rss>